# expect: `on key` listens to the document, not to `Column`
#
# The misreading this refuses: `on key` indented under an element looks
# like the `on click` beside it and is not — it fires for a keystroke
# aimed anywhere on the page, including at a field inside some other
# element entirely. Position decides its lifetime and nothing else, so
# it is written beside the elements rather than under one.
state n is client Whole starting 0
view
    Column
        Text n
        on key "Escape"
            add 1 to n
